-- title:
--   Constants of A=A₀[ζ_A] lie in the image of `classify`
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell$ a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity for which some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ sends $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22), the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell)^\times$; let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L$ inside the Laurent series field over $L$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be a nonzero element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal $(q)$ and finite residue field, mapping to $A$ and to $K$ compatibly, containing a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity, and with $\ell$ and $M'$ invertible in $A_0$. Assume: the three equivariance hypotheses `hℓ`, `hM`, `hL` (stability of `IsGamma1Point` at $\ell$, of `IsGamma0PowAt` and of divisibility of `inLineMulPoly` under variable change); group laws $\mathcal{G}$ on the projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras which are chord–tangent and have the origin as identity; a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ for Drinfeld $q$-bases satisfying `IsSectionTransport`; and the hypotheses `hVC`, `hCO` producing graded ring homomorphisms on the projective model rings realising variable changes and coefficient maps. Let $D$ be the level moduli datum of `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓ M' q hℓ hM hL 𝒢 𝒯`, whose points over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ are Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant equipped with a $\Gamma_0$-type polynomial for each prime power $p^{v_p(M')}$, $p \mid M'$, a `LevelPData` which is a $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-point, and a Drinfeld $q$-basis, subject to the linkage `IsGamma1Link`, all taken up to variable change, with $j$-invariant as the $j$-map. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for $D$ over $A_0$, that is an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$, of finite type over $A_0$, with a universal point such that every point of $D$ over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is obtained from it by a unique $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $B_0 \to T$. Let $x$ be a point of $D$ over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has Laurent expansion [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18), and let $\zeta_A \in A$ satisfy $\zeta_A^q = 1$ and $A_0[\zeta_A] = A$. Then for every $a \in A$ there is $b \in B_0$ whose image under the classifying homomorphism of $x$ is the image of $a$ in $K$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity-onto-constants step for the Tate point in the $\Gamma_1(\ell)$-framed rigid full-level moduli problem: over an unramified base $A_0$ with finite residue field and $A = A_0[\zeta_A]$ generated by a $q$-th root of unity, all of $A$ is reached by the classifying map of the point $x$ with $j$-invariant the $q$-expansion `jqNModC L q`. It feeds the `AuxLevelOne` constructions identifying the adic completion of the relevant stalk and the action of the level automorphisms there.
